WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.334
(Light whimsical music)

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.848
- When I'd go to compete, I'd realize

00:00:03.848 --> 00:00:08.046
there's not a lot of
people who look like me.

00:00:08.046 --> 00:00:10.872
There's an opportunity here to encourage

00:00:10.872 --> 00:00:13.289
and teach people how to sail.

00:00:14.277 --> 00:00:15.844
My name is Ayme Sinclair.

00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:18.489
I'm a sailor, and I'm
trying to open up sailing

00:00:18.489 --> 00:00:20.539
so that it's a more diverse sport.

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:23.968
(Whimsical music)

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.037
(Waves crashing)

00:00:26.037 --> 00:00:27.037
Turn. Ready?

00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:30.070
Alright. Everybody ready?

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.036
Tacking!

00:00:31.036 --> 00:00:34.869
(cable pulled through pulley)

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.742
I got into sailing four years ago.

00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:42.491
I had a moment where I
was just really unhappy.

00:00:42.491 --> 00:00:44.876
And the idea that I was able to come out

00:00:44.876 --> 00:00:47.577
every Wednesday night and
sail with my teammates

00:00:47.577 --> 00:00:50.152
was like my one place of happiness.

00:00:50.152 --> 00:00:51.869
And I loved that.

00:00:51.869 --> 00:00:54.567
It saved me when I was
in a really dark place.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.102
Pull.

00:00:56.102 --> 00:00:58.722
The team that I race with
now is called Sweet Caroline.

00:00:58.722 --> 00:01:00.060
I love my teammates.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.728
They're my family.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.620
Half the team is women.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.441
We represent eight different countries,

00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:09.858
from Morocco to Peru, Jamaica,
to Columbia and India.

00:01:11.392 --> 00:01:13.826
But, when I would go
to compete, I'd realize

00:01:13.826 --> 00:01:16.062
we're the only team that looks like us.

00:01:16.062 --> 00:01:18.540
Jay, can you put this in the locker?

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.843
One of the things that I wanted to do

00:01:19.843 --> 00:01:23.307
was start a collective
channel called Sailing Noire,

00:01:23.307 --> 00:01:24.175
an Instagram account,

00:01:24.175 --> 00:01:26.352
so that I can get the word out about it

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.371
and encourage more people to join.

00:01:28.371 --> 00:01:29.827
It wound up taking off,

00:01:29.827 --> 00:01:31.875
a lot of people started
following and reaching out,

00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:33.761
asking how they can learn.

00:01:33.761 --> 00:01:36.192
I realized that there's
an opportunity here

00:01:36.192 --> 00:01:39.697
to encourage and teach people how to sail.

00:01:39.697 --> 00:01:42.579
So then I started traveling.

00:01:42.579 --> 00:01:44.504
Hi, so my name is Ayme.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.579
I am a competitive sailor from New York.

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:48.755
I would put together
different groups of people,

00:01:48.755 --> 00:01:51.363
and we would go out and we
would sail for a couple days.

00:01:51.363 --> 00:01:53.230
More recently, I went to Kenya.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.566
I put together the first
ever women's sailing team.

00:01:56.566 --> 00:01:58.326
And it was amazing.

00:01:58.326 --> 00:02:03.326
- (woman) The first all-female
sailing team competing.

00:02:03.595 --> 00:02:06.095
- One...two...three...winning!

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.555
- I decided we're going
to start a women's team;

00:02:09.555 --> 00:02:11.275
we're going to join this race;

00:02:11.275 --> 00:02:14.304
and we're going to show these
girls that they can do this.

00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:16.776
And help these girls feel like they were

00:02:16.776 --> 00:02:19.339
empowered to learn something new.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.801
It was probably one of
the most amazing things

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.636
I've ever experienced in my life.

00:02:23.636 --> 00:02:25.576
There were all these
women from this community

00:02:25.576 --> 00:02:26.926
who never come out,

00:02:26.926 --> 00:02:28.754
don't participate in sailing or boating,

00:02:28.754 --> 00:02:31.056
which is two of the biggest drivers

00:02:31.056 --> 00:02:33.726
of the economy on that island.

00:02:33.726 --> 00:02:36.464
We changed the way a whole
community thinks about

00:02:36.464 --> 00:02:38.464
women's role in society.

00:02:39.326 --> 00:02:42.179
(Seagulls squawking) (Waves crashing)

00:02:42.179 --> 00:02:45.231
(light whimsical music)

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.875
I think sailing should be
more inclusive and diverse,

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.986
because it's such a loss that

00:02:49.986 --> 00:02:52.624
other people don't get to experience

00:02:52.624 --> 00:02:54.681
the same thing that I do.

00:02:54.681 --> 00:02:56.256
They're just not use to seeing us.

00:02:56.256 --> 00:02:57.305
So we gotta fix that.

00:02:57.305 --> 00:02:59.224
(Light whimsical music)

00:02:59.224 --> 00:03:01.175
I would say try something new,

00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:02.590
don't be afraid.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:05.389
You will surprise yourself
when you realize you can do it.

00:03:05.389 --> 00:03:07.890
And that feeling, you
can't put a price on that.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.223
(Light whimsical music)

